<%# ONE COMPARISON CELL: included, or genuinely not.

  The mark carries sr-only text because here it IS the cell's content -- unlike the card's tick, which sits
  beside a label. An unmarked "not included" cell would read as a cell nobody filled in, which is a
  different claim from a capability this plan does not sell.

  The excluded mark is a line rather than a cross: at this size a cross reads as an error, and a plan not
  including something is not one.
%>
<% if included %>
  <span class="inline-flex items-center text-lyn-indigo">
    <span class="sr-only"><%= t('marketing.pricing.included') %></span>
    <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-5" fill="none"
         stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
      <path d="m20 6-11 11-5-5"/>
    </svg>
  </span>
<% else %>
  <span class="inline-flex items-center text-lyn-ink-soft/40">
    <span class="sr-only"><%= t('marketing.pricing.not_included') %></span>
    <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-5" fill="none"
         stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round">
      <path d="M6 12h12"/>
    </svg>
  </span>
<% end %>
